{"id":"6995a2a16a371000130df7e9","slug":"james-turrell-gathas-curved-glass-series-1","title":"Gathas (Curved Glass Series)","artists":["James Turrell"],"date":"2019","medium":"Computerized LED","dimensions":"2/5 × 2/5 × 2/5 in","image":"6z9RR8p3P2wPl6rqZppxpg","c":["#190763","#4e1dcb","#170325"],"said":[{"k":"note","q":"The work from the «Curved Glass» type – a horizontal elliptical shape – has a brightly colored aperture that appears unfathomable between plane, volume and infinite depth. The view loses itself in the barely noticeably changing color moods which follow a detailed program and which could just as well be complementary contrasts and afterimages that the eye generates itself.","by":"Häusler Contemporary, on Artsy"}],"events":[{"k":"made","y":"2019","q":"2019","o":1,"s":[0]},{"k":"exhibited","y":"2019","t":"James Turrell - Passages of Light","v":"Museo Jumex","q":"James Turrell - Passages of Light, Museo Jumex, 2019","ll":[19.3208,-99.1515],"w":"Mexico City, MX","p":"mexico-city-mx","pr":"city","o":1,"s":[1]},{"k":"listed","y":"2026-02-18","who":"Häusler Contemporary","n":"listed by the gallery","ll":[47.3809,8.5422],"w":"Zurich, CH","p":"zurich-ch","pr":"office","o":2,"s":[0]},{"k":"owned","who":"Studio James Turrell","q":"Studio James Turrell","o":1,"s":[1]}],"sources":[{"name":"Artsy","url":"https://www.artsy.net/artwork/james-turrell-gathas-curved-glass-series-1"},{"name":"Häusler Contemporary, on Artsy","url":"https://www.artsy.net/artwork/james-turrell-gathas-curved-glass-series-1"}],"threads":[{"id":"bdb2839d","k":"artist","name":"James Turrell","y":2019,"n":35}],"asof":"2026-10-01"}